On 18.03.2016 21:49, Stafford Horne wrote:
> Hello,
> 
> Just testing if this new list is ready and working, are there any
> other memebers?  Also, wanted to say Hi and introduce myself.
> 
> I have been talkative in the #openrisc channel recently, so most 
> probably know me. But, I would like to talk a bit about my
> background in case someone cares: - Studied Computer Engineering in
> University - Learned RTL design + verilog there (>10 years ago) -
> No problem with vhdl either - Kept an interest in hardware but have
> a job in software - In the past few years I have started to really
> get back into hardware design (both analog and digital). I designed
> a very simple sdram controller in verilog for the de0 nano. I
> hooked up a self designed preamp circuit, dac chip and amp to the
> de0 nano and built a small digital recorder (all hardware, all on
> github, and demo on youtube) - I then looked into running linux on
> the de0 nano and found OpenRISC.
> 
> Thats how I am here. Thats the hardware side; software side is I am
> OSS advocate and have worked on a few projects here and there for
> the past 15 years.
> 
> -Stafford

Hi Stafford,

thanks for the introduction. There are a few members on this list now,
I will crosspost all future posts to lists.opencores.org here, so that
we hopefully switch over here soon.

Thanks for your great work so far, very much appreciated. Welcome to
the OpenRISC community!

Cheers,
Stefan

